{
  "_id": "6af264c3be2268deb4a38b01",
  "Package": "MRManalyzeR",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "Process and Analyse Targeted LC-MS Lipidomics and Metabolomics\nData",
  "Version": "0.99.10",
  "Authors@R": "c(\nperson(\"Matthew J.\", \"Smith\",\nemail = \"mattyjsmith123@gmail.com\",\nrole = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"),\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-7357-2670\")),\nperson(\"Antonio\", \"Checa\",\nrole = \"aut\",\ncomment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-0674-3329\")))",
  "Description": "Reproducible post-acquisition processing of targeted\nLC-MS/MS lipidomics and metabolomics results exported from\nWaters TargetLynx or from Skyline, or supplied as a plain\nsample-by-analyte matrix. Reads the quantitative result tables,\nintegrates them with sample and feature metadata, and applies\nconfigurable signal filtering (SNR, LOD or LOQ), blank\nfiltering, batch correction, normalisation, internal-standard\nand volume adjustment of vendor-reported concentrations, and\nmissing-value imputation. Each step is an exported function\nacting on a struct DatasetExperiment; a complete workflow can\nadditionally be driven from a single YAML configuration via\nrunMRManalyzeR(), which also renders self-contained HTML\ndata-quality and statistical reports. Chromatographic peak\ndetection, peak integration and calibration-curve fitting from\nraw mass-spectrometry data are outside its scope.",
  "License": "MIT + file LICENSE",
  "Encoding": "UTF-8",
  "biocViews": "Metabolomics, Lipidomics, MassSpectrometry, QualityControl,\nNormalization, BatchEffect, Visualization, WorkflowStep",
